WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.145
Every vehicle in your stock already has what it needs for its own listing video:

2
00:00:06.145 --> 00:00:11.215
photos, specification, mileage, fuel type, transmission and price.

3
00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:17.591
A narrated walkthrough is built from those assets in the order a buyer would use on

4
00:00:17.591 --> 00:00:23.813
the forecourt — exterior first, then interior, odometer, boot, engine bay and any

5
00:00:23.813 --> 00:00:25.426
marks shown honestly.

6
00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:31.657
Because the material exists for every unit, not only the headline cars, every unit

7
00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:32.949
can have a video.

8
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:38.770
Two cuts come from one set of photos: a vertical cut for social and a landscape cut

9
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.645
for a website gallery or YouTube channel.

10
00:00:41.645 --> 00:00:46.765
When a price changes, the video is re-rendered against the updated listing.

11
00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:50.306
When a vehicle sells, the video is retired.

12
00:00:50.306 --> 00:00:55.565
Stock turns over, and a video tied to a stock number turns over with it.
